WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.511
This one is for the night you wake up with your heart already going.

00:00:04.461 --> 00:00:07.005
Not a slow drift into worry.

00:00:07.005 --> 00:00:11.270
You are awake and the alarm is on before you have a single thought.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.667
The thought arrives second, and it arrives looking like a reason.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.755
That order matters, so hold on to it.

00:00:18.755 --> 00:00:20.623
The body went first.

00:00:20.623 --> 00:00:33.152
What is running now is a surge that was already scheduled, cortisol and adrenaline climbing towards morning, landing on whatever is unfinished in your life and lighting it up.

00:00:33.152 --> 00:00:39.652
At three in the morning you have the full stress response and none of the daytime brain that argues back.

00:00:39.652 --> 00:00:44.961
So everything looks worse, and the worse it looks, the more alert you get.

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:47.858
The thoughts are louder, not truer.

00:00:47.858 --> 00:00:53.505
You are not going to decide anything tonight, and nothing here needs deciding tonight.

00:00:53.505 --> 00:00:56.005
So we do not start with the mind.

00:00:56.005 --> 00:00:57.873
We start with the chest.

00:00:57.873 --> 00:01:06.108
Breathe in through your nose, a normal breath, then on top of it take a second short sip of air through the nose.

00:01:06.108 --> 00:01:11.417
Then let it all go out through your mouth, slowly, longer than the way in.

00:01:11.417 --> 00:01:12.594
Again.

00:01:12.594 --> 00:01:18.682
Normal breath in, second short sip on top, and a long slow release.

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:36.823
Again, and this time make the out breath last as long as it can without straining.

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:51.042
Twice more, on your own.

00:02:21.148 --> 00:02:27.118
That double breath is the fastest way down that does not need you to feel calm first.

00:02:27.068 --> 00:02:32.348
It works on a racing heart, and it works whether or not you believe it will.

00:02:40.516 --> 00:02:44.148
Now the part that decides how long this lasts.

00:02:44.098 --> 00:02:46.274
Do not argue with the thought.

00:02:46.274 --> 00:02:54.304
Do not check anything to reassure yourself, no phone, no email, no bank app, no symptom search.

00:02:54.304 --> 00:02:59.230
Reassurance at three in the morning is the strongest fuel this thing has.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:04.333
It works for about ninety seconds and then the question comes back bigger.

00:03:04.333 --> 00:03:09.907
Instead, name it once, in one sentence, and hand it to daylight.

00:03:09.907 --> 00:03:12.024
Say it in your head like this.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:17.024
This is the three AM version of a real thing, and I will look at it at eight.

00:03:17.024 --> 00:03:19.730
Then get out of bed if the alert stays.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:25.098
Chair, low light, something over your shoulders, paper and pen.

00:03:25.098 --> 00:03:33.171
Write it down until the loop goes quiet, and put one line at the bottom, the smallest thing you can do about it tomorrow.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:39.560
Then read something boring until your eyes are closing on their own, and go back to bed only then.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.775
Tomorrow, three things.

00:04:41.775 --> 00:04:45.598
Normal wake time, no matter what tonight gave you.

00:04:45.598 --> 00:04:49.451
Ten minutes of outdoor light in the first half hour.

00:04:49.451 --> 00:04:55.804
And the sentence you wrote, looked at properly, in daylight, when you have a brain to look at it with.

00:04:55.804 --> 00:04:59.392
One night like this is a spike, not a return.

00:04:59.392 --> 00:05:07.657
If your chest is doing this most nights, or if the fear is running in the daytime too, that is worth a conversation with a doctor.

00:05:07.657 --> 00:05:15.319
This is coaching, not medical care, and there is a version of this that is treatable and is not about sleep at all.

00:05:15.319 --> 00:05:18.495
For tonight, nothing is required of you.

00:05:18.495 --> 00:05:21.319
The surge peaks, then it falls.

00:05:21.319 --> 00:05:23.128
It always falls.
